From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi7: 061 0x07 之后把环重建一遍再发启动命令

With the finish moved after the RAM code the download runs to the end: all
five regions are fetched, didx walks 0->98, the RAM chunks land where the
headers ask for, PATCH_FINISH_REQ is answered - and then the start command
sits in the ring unanswered until mtk_mcu_tx_nocheck gives up:

  diag ram region4: addr=0x00407200 len=80 feature=0x01 mode=0x80000089
  diag cmd push: len=76 ... didx=98
  diag: late patch finish -> 0
  diag cmd push: len=72 head=101 tail=100 didx=100
  Failed to start WM firmware

PATCH_FINISH_REQ is what hands the chip to the firmware, and the firmware
clears the PCIe config while it comes up (cmd=0x0000, bar0 back to its reset
value, lpctl=0).  In the early-finish flow that does not hurt because the core
rebuilds the rings between the patch and the start phase - the log shows the
endpoint recovered and the rings rebuilt about 4 s later, right before the RAM
request.  This driver now queues the start command straight after the finish,
into rings the receiver has already forgotten.

diag_reinit_after_patch (on by default) calls the same bus init the core calls
after the patch phase, once the finish has been acknowledged, and only then
queues MCU_CMD_FW_START_REQ.  diag_start_delay_ms adds an optional pause
between the rebuild and the start command for the case where the firmware
needs longer to come up.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
---
--- a/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
+++ b/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
@@ -332,6 +332,24 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_late_patch_finish,
 		 "send PATCH_FINISH_REQ after the RAM code instead of before it");
 
+/*
+ * 061: PATCH_FINISH_REQ hands the chip over to the firmware and the firmware
+ * clears the PCIe config on its way up, so the rings that carried the download
+ * are gone by the time the start command is queued.  The core rebuilds them
+ * between the patch and the start phase, which is why the early finish works
+ * up to the point where the download window closes; do the same rebuild here
+ * now that the finish moved after the RAM code.
+ */
+static bool diag_reinit_after_patch = true;
+module_param(diag_reinit_after_patch, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_reinit_after_patch,
+		 "rebuild the bus rings after PATCH_FINISH_REQ, before the start command");
+
+static unsigned int diag_start_delay_ms;
+module_param(diag_start_delay_ms, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_start_delay_ms,
+		 "sleep this long after the rebuild and before the start command");
+
 static int
 mcu_wm_load_patch(struct mtk_hw_dev *dev, struct mtk_mcu_entry *mcu_entry)
 {
@@ -649,6 +667,20 @@
 		dev_err(dev->dev, "diag: late patch finish -> %d\n", err);
 		if (err)
 			return err;
+
+		if (diag_reinit_after_patch) {
+			err = mtk_bus_dma_init_device(dev->bus_trans);
+			dev_err(dev->dev, "diag: dma re-init after patch -> %d\n",
+				err);
+			if (err)
+				return err;
+		}
+
+		if (diag_start_delay_ms) {
+			dev_info(dev->dev, "diag: waiting %u ms before start\n",
+				 diag_start_delay_ms);
+			msleep(diag_start_delay_ms);
+		}
 	}
 
 	return mcu_wm_start_firmware(dev, override, option);
